/P 260 0 R
/E (Credit scoring models, such as those created by FICO, often factor in the age of your oldest account and the average age of all your accounts, rewarding individuals with longer credit histories. Before you close an account, think about your credit history. It may be beneficial to leave the account open once you have paid it off.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
418 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 260 0 R
/E (Of course, if keeping accounts open and having available credit could trigger additional spending and debt, it might be more beneficial to close the accounts. Make sure you carefully evaluate your situation; only you know what can work best for your financial outlook.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
