/P 261 0 R
/E (When these accounts report on your credit records, they are coded very specifically so that not only consumers and lenders but also credit scoring models can easily identify them. Statistical analysis has determined that the type of accounts you have is predictive of your future credit risk.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
422 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 261 0 R
/E (So what does all of this mean to you, the consumer? Consumers with the strongest credit scores, including FICO credit scores, tend to have a mix of different types of accounts. Of course, the key is to manage these accounts responsibly. Credit scoring models look to see if you can handle different types of financing as they assess your creditworthiness.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
